---

<EventPageLayout
  lang={lang}
  pageKey="misteri-procida"
  metaTitle={"Misteri of Procida 2027: The Good Friday Procession"}
  metaDescription={"The procession of the Misteri in Procida on 26 March 2027: the cortege leaves at dawn from Terra Murata with the Mysteries built by the islanders and the hooded brothers of the Turchini."}
  breadcrumbs={breadcrumbs}
  hero={hero}
  schema={schema}
  facts={facts}
  transport={transport}
  slider={slider}
  relatedEvents={relatedEvents}
  cta={cta}
>
  <p slot="intro">Procida's Good Friday procession began as a penitential cortege and is one of the strongest identity rituals in the Bay of Naples: the earliest documented record goes back to 1688. Originally the brothers of the Turchini practised self flagellation; when the Counter-Reformation banned those displays, the symbols of the Passion carried in procession took their place.</p>
  <p slot="intro">The Misteri are works built each year by the islanders, large sculptural and scenic groups drawn from the Old and New Testament. Some themes are fixed, others change from year to year, and hundreds of people work on them for months. In 2027 Easter falls on 28 March, so Good Friday is the 26th.</p>

  <div>
    <h3 class="font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900 mb-6">How it unfolds</h3>
    <div class="grid sm:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">Dawn</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">The start at Terra Murata</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">At first light on Good Friday the Misteri are lined up on the esplanade of Terra Murata, next to the Abbey of San Michele Arcangelo. After the call of the oldest member of the Turchini, the order of the cortege is set according to the religious theme each one represents.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="bg-white p-8 rounded-[2rem] border border-slate-100 shadow-sm">
        <span class="text-med-gold text-[10px] font-bold uppercase tracking-widest mb-2 block">The descent</span>
        <h4 class="text-xl font-serif font-bold text-slate-900 mb-3">Down to the harbour and across the island</h4>
        <p class="text-slate-600 text-xs sm:text-sm leading-relaxed">The cortege comes down from the fortified village and crosses the island. It lasts several hours and it is the one day of the year when Procida, almost deserted out of season, fills up. In the evening comes the solemn Way of the Cross and the return of the statues.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

</EventPageLayout>
